---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import atlas from "../../data/atlas.json";
---

<Base
  title="About this atlas"
  description="What Product Leaders Atlas is, how to share it, and how cards are made."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About this atlas</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A public English map of how product orgs actually operate — and how they
      disagree. One sharp thesis per company; compare ownership, craft, and
      stage.
    </p>

    <h2>Why it exists</h2>
    <p>
      Most interview notes die in notebooks. This project turns Product Leaders
      conversations into sparse company cards you can scan in twenty seconds and
      stack against peers. The goal is contrast, not coverage theater.
    </p>

    <h2>What’s on the map</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>{atlas.company_count}</strong> published orgs on the
        <a href="/">map</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>{atlas.weak_count || 0}</strong> held as weak (soft thesis,
        theory, or unstable org signal)
      </li>
      <li>
        Compare any two or three on <a href="/compare">/compare</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        Or start from curated arguments on <a href="/tensions">/tensions</a>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Share</h2>
    <p>
      Link the map, a company card, or a compare URL. Cards are original
      English synthesis — not transcripts. Source episode titles stay in
      Spanish as muted labels.
    </p>
    <p class="share-blurb">
      Product Leaders Atlas — how real product orgs operate, one thesis per
      company. Compare ownership, loops, and stage.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Map: <a href="https://product-leaders-self.vercel.app/"
          >product-leaders-self.vercel.app</a
        >
      </li>
      <li>
        Sample compare:{" "}
        <a
          href="https://product-leaders-self.vercel.app/compare?a=cabify&amp;b=shakers&amp;c=webel"
          >Cabify vs Shakers vs Webel</a
        >
      </li>
      <li>
        Repo:
        <a href="https://github.com/Angelguirao/product-leaders"
          >github.com/Angelguirao/product-leaders</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How cards are made</h2>
    <p>
      Catalog → extract → LLM brief → quality gate → index. Only
      <strong>published</strong> cards appear on the map. Read
      <a href="/docs/how-to-read">how to read a card</a> and
      <a href="/docs/legal">legal notes</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Source</h2>
    <p>
      Seeded from Dani Diestre’s
      <a href="https://podcasters.spotify.com/pod/show/danidiestre"
        >Entrevistas a Product Leaders</a
      >. Unofficial. Not affiliated.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
